# oracle: angle amoeba (Tinker sextic angle, bond-angle cross term and Urey-Bradley 1-3 term) on the AMOEBA water dimer, read from its full data file (Angle Coeffs # amoeba, BondAngle Coeffs, UreyBradley Coeffs); bond class2 (the example's bond style). The pair style is zero: only the bonded energies (eangle, ebond) and forces are compared
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_full.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 skip=press
# press is skipped: the shrink-wrapped volume of boundary s s s differs from native by about 1.2e-7 relative (see w119amoeba_hal)
units           real
boundary        s s s
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_full.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      zero 3.0
pair_coeff      * *
thermo_style    custom step ebond eangle edihed eimp emol pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
